From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:58:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Dolby Vision: the bridge at the display mode's size

The Vulkan engine's canvas is a run-time size now (dvvk_create_canvas):
the private scanout buffers, the GUI raster the engine reads (shared, or
its copy) and the pictures' placement take the size of the output the
bridge was begun for instead of 3840x2160. Nothing changes for the
Dolby Vision tunnel and its HDR10 conversions, which the window only
begins at 3840x2160; the SDR output that follows runs at any mode whose
width and height the engine takes.

An engine library without dvvk_create_canvas is asked for 3840x2160
with dvvk_create as before, and refused for another size.
